==============================================================
 TEXTURES IN THE MATERIAL LANGUAGE
==============================================================

-- 1. What the author writes, and what it becomes ------------
   color tint
   texture skin
   {
     let t = sample(skin, @uv)
     @out = t * tint * (@lambert * 0.8 + 0.2)
   }

   became:
     var t_skin : texture_2d<f32>   [emitted]

Line 369 Haro refused this statement (bare name is not a local (Rule A) `nOk`, line 369 of gg5_texture.ring) and did not compile it -- running past it would give a wrong answer